WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.440
Welcome back to Models &amp; Agents Episode F-D-5 on May 21, 2026.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:10.280
Let's see what shipped. Let's see what happened in the AI world today,

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:15.200
and trust me, it's been busy. A general-purpose reasoning model just

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:21.180
disproved an 80-year-old math conjecture by finding better constructions than the square grid's

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:26.440
mathematicians expected. Open AI announced that one of its general-purpose models

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:31.800
solved the planar unit distance problem posed by Paul Erduce in 1946.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:37.980
This marks the first time AI has autonomously resolved a prominent open math question.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:43.420
The model discovered an entirely new family of constructions that outperformed the square

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:49.480
grid patterns long assumed to be optimal. The result came from a model not specialized for math.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:56.220
It maintained long chains of reasoning across distant concepts and surfaced previously unexplored paths.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:02.040
Open AI notes that the same systems will soon accelerate work in biology, physics,

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:07.760
and medicine, while still requiring human judgment to choose problems and interpret outcomes.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:13.540
Developers should watch for follow-up papers and whether similar reasoning gains appear in

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:20.040
coding or scientific tool use benchmarks. Now let's move to the model updates that landed this week.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:28.720
Demis Haasabis highlighted that Gemini 3.5-flash outperformed the prior 3.1-pro on coding and

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:36.020
agentic tasks. The model runs four times faster than other frontier models. It reaches 800 tokens per

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:43.340
second in anti-gravity. Gemini 3.5-flash also ships at less than half the cost of comparable systems.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:49.900
A pro variant is still coming. Builders working on latency sensitive agents or high volume coding

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:56.420
workflows should test it immediately in the Gemini app or anti-gravity. Haasabis pointed to the

00:01:56.420 --> 00:02:02.640
official Google blog post for deeper technical details on the new Flash model. The release continues

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.680
Google's push to deliver faster, cheaper inference optimized for agent workloads.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:14.900
Let's turn to the agent and tool developments. Resolve AI expanded its platform with a coordinated

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:21.680
team of specialized agents. These agents pursue multiple hypotheses in parallel, cross-verify

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:28.580
conclusions, and build full causal chains for production incidents. The new architecture reportedly doubles

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:35.060
root cause accuracy on internal benchmarks. It includes always on background agents plus a shared

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:42.380
workspace for human agent collaboration. Engineering teams can integrate it via REST API or MCP

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:49.140
server and pay only for actual troubleshooting work. Corei.ai launched the Artemis edition of its

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:56.140
agent platform. The platform centers on a YAML-based agent blueprint language. An AI architect called

00:02:56.140 --> 00:03:01.800
ARCH translates natural language requirements into deployable, governed, multi-agent systems.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:08.880
The platform uses a dual-brain architecture that pairs LLM reasoning with deterministic business

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:15.000
rule execution. It supports 175 models across clouds and on-premises.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:22.080
Existing customers are already planning migrations while new deployments start on the updated stack.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:29.420
Ripletide introduced decision context graphs that give agents structured memory, time-aware reasoning,

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:36.360
and explicit decision logic. The graphs make agents non-regressive so they can compound validated

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:42.940
action sequences over time. The approach encodes applicability rules and temporal validity directly

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:49.180
rather than relying on the model to infer them. On the practical and community side, LLM station

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:56.540
reached version 0.9. It is a Windows GUI that launches LLMOS server directly with full parameter

00:03:56.540 --> 00:04:05.160
control. The tool supports multiple backends including official LLMA.CPP with MTP, TurboQuant for high

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:11.060
context KV cache quantization, and voice features via XTTS and faster whisper.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:22.540
Users report strong results running 23.627b at 177 kilobytes context on dual RTX 3060 cards.

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:29.400
The project retains real-time VRAM monitoring and per model profiles. The project is open-source

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:37.220
under MIT and accepts contributions for Linux and Mac ports. The LLM planner site helps users match

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:44.220
rigs to models or models to existing hardware. It covers more than 60 builds and more than 50 models.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:51.880
The site sites more than 130 talk for S sources and links more than 150 reviewer videos.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:56.500
It includes decode and prompt processing speeds at multiple quants,

00:04:56.500 --> 00:05:04.280
power draw, and multi-region pricing with weekly updates. A user running LLMA 370B locally with

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:10.980
function calling is seeking cheap or free APIs that return useful web page chunks. The thread

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:16.280
surfaces practical trade-offs between context quality and costs for local agent setups.

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:23.360
Okay, let's pop the hood on multi-agent verification loops. Everyone talks about multi-agent systems

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:30.200
as if simply adding more models will automatically improve reliability. In practice, verification works

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:35.820
through explicit hand-off protocols. One agent must cite every evidence fragment it used.

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:42.520
Another agent is tasked with attempting to disprove the proposed causal chain. This adds measurable

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:50.240
latency, often 200-400 milliseconds per verification round, yet it dramatically reduces confident but

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:56.360
unsupported conclusions on complex incidents. The key engineering choice is deciding how many

00:05:56.360 --> 00:06:01.680
independent hypotheses to explore in parallel versus how deeply to verify each one.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:09.420
Teams that oververify see diminishing returns once accuracy plateaus, around 85-90% on their

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:16.360
internal eVal sets. When the cost of a wrong route causes high, the architecture shines. When speed

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:22.500
matters more than perfect explanations, a single well-prompted agent with strong retrieval still wins.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:29.000
The gacha that bites most teams is forgetting to let agents explicitly say I do not have enough

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:35.240
evidence. That turns the system back into a confident hallucinator. Here are the things to try this

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:43.240
week. Test Gemini 3.5 Flash in the Gemini app or anti-gravity for coding and agentic tasks to see the

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:51.420
reported four-time speed and sub-half-cost gains firsthand. Spin up Lama Station version 0.9 if you

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:58.860
run Lama.cpp on Windows and want full parameter control plus turboquant high-contact support without

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:06.020
command line overhead. Experiment with Resolve AI's MCP server integration so your existing coding

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:10.840
agents can hand off production debugging to the multi-agent investigation system.

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:18.360
Explore Coray.ai's Artemis platform on Azure if you need declarative agent definitions that combine

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:24.640
LLM reasoning with deterministic business rules for regulated environments. Compare the

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:30.920
RIPLIT TIDE decision context graph approach against plain rag when building agents that must respect

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:37.740
time-scoped policies and avoid regression on repeated tasks. On the horizon, open AI is

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:43.280
expected to release further details and papers on the general purpose reasoning techniques behind

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:50.340
the Erdos result. Google will continue rolling out Gemini 3.5 Flash capabilities and the promised

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:57.560
pro variant. More enterprise agent platforms are likely to announce MCP and rest interoperability

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:03.860
as the pattern becomes standard for agent to agent hand off. Hardware vendors and open source projects

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:11.180
will keep shipping new backends and quantization methods aimed at 100K plus context on consumer GPUs.

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:16.940
Tomorrow, keep an eye on the first follow-up papers from open AI on the reasoning techniques

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:23.500
that cracked the old math problem. That wraps up today's AI briefing. Share this with a developer

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:28.240
or builder who wants to stay current. Subscribe wherever you listen. See you tomorrow.

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:35.460
This episode used AI voice synthesis of my voice. Editorial selection and analysis are my own.
